The work didn't achieve its intended effect. The receivables entry for INV-2026-1354 shows € 684.99, but the work item says the invoice is for € 6,849.86. That is roughly a tenth of the correct amount, and the cents don't match either (684.99 against 684.986). The invoice is marked SENT to K-50, so the customer was probably billed the wrong amount.

The other entries look normal. The CRM shows the invoice email going to K-50 with the PDF attached, the PDF is archived, and a dunning reminder is scheduled. The "All checks green" report doesn't hold up, because it missed the amount error. The amount in the posted invoice or the PDF needs checking and correcting. I didn't look anything up in the runbook, since the amount mismatch alone settles the verdict.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.93, "reason": "Posted receivable for INV-2026-1354 is € 684.99, not the requested € 6,849.86, so the customer was billed the wrong amount."}

The runbook says D1 has 100 known duplicate respondents. The report shows only 43 removed (24,015 − 23,972 = 43). That leaves about 57 duplicates in the file. The weight total (2,195,342) and the column count (61) match the runbook. The female share also matches the census figure.

The work item required removing duplicate respondents, and that was only partly done. The report also lists no check for the income code -9, though that code is not shown to be a problem.

